I'll help you create a selection context menu feature for ChatEntry. This will allow users to right-click on selected text and see actions like "Copy" and "Create sub-task".

I'll need to create a new component for the context menu. Let me first ask for clarification on one missing piece:

**Missing Context:**
1. What specific actions should be available in the selection menu? (I see "Copy" and "Create sub-task" mentioned - should there be more like "Search", "Highlight", etc.?)
2. Should the context menu appear on right-click, or also on text selection with a floating toolbar?
3. For "Create sub-task", what data should be passed with the emit event?

For now, I'll implement a solution with the actions you mentioned. Here are the files:

## New Selection Context Menu Component

```vue src/components/SelectionMenu.vue
<script setup>
</script>

<template>
  <div 
    v-if="isVisible"
    class="fixed bg-base-100 rounded-lg shadow-lg border border-base-300 z-50 py-2 min-w-48"
    :style="{ top: menuPosition.y + 'px', left: menuPosition.x + 'px' }"
    @mousedown.stop
  >
    <button 
      class="w-full px-4 py-2 text-left hover:bg-base-200 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm"
      @click="onCopy"
    >
      <i class="fa-solid fa-copy"></i>
      Copy
    </button>
    <button 
      class="w-full px-4 py-2 text-left hover:bg-base-200 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm"
      @click="onCreateSubtask"
    >
      <i class="fa-solid fa-list-check"></i>
      Create sub-task
    </button>
    <div class="divider my-1"></div>
    <button 
      class="w-full px-4 py-2 text-left hover:bg-base-200 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm"
      @click="onClose"
    >
      <i class="fa-solid fa-times"></i>
      Close
    </button>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    selectedText: { type: String, default: '' },
    position: { type: Object, default: () => ({ x: 0, y: 0 }) },
    isVisible: { type: Boolean, default: false }
  },
  emits: ['copy', 'create-subtask', 'close'],
  data() {
    return {
      menuPosition: { x: 0, y: 0 }
    }
  },
  watch: {
    position(newPos) {
      this.menuPosition = { ...newPos }
    },
    isVisible(visible) {
      if (visible) {
        document.addEventListener('click', this.closeMenu)
        document.addEventListener('contextmenu', this.closeMenu)
      } else {
        document.removeEventListener('click', this.closeMenu)
        document.removeEventListener('contextmenu', this.closeMenu)
      }
    }
  },
  beforeUnmount() {
    document.removeEventListener('click', this.closeMenu)
    document.removeEventListener('contextmenu', this.closeMenu)
  },
  methods: {
    onCopy() {
      this.$emit('copy', this.selectedText)
      this.onClose()
    },
    onCreateSubtask() {
      this.$emit('create-subtask', this.selectedText)
      this.onClose()
    },
    onClose() {
      this.$emit('close')
    },
    closeMenu() {
      this.onClose()
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Updated ChatEntry.vue

Now integrate the SelectionMenu into ChatEntry.vue. Add this to the imports in `<script setup>`:

```vue src/components/ChatEntry.vue
<script setup>
import Markdown from './Markdown.vue'
import moment from 'moment'
import { CodeDiff } from 'v-code-diff'
import ChatIcon from './chat/ChatIcon.vue'
import Document from './document/Document.vue'
import UserSelector from './chat/UserSelector.vue'
import ProfileAvatar from './profile/ProfileAvatar.vue'
import ChatEntryMobile from './ChatEntryMobile.vue'
import DocumentSummary from './document/DocumentSummary.vue'
import MessagePRView from './chat/MessagePRView.vue'
import SelectionMenu from './SelectionMenu.vue'
</script>
```

Then add the SelectionMenu component to the template (add this right after the opening `<div v-else>` in the desktop rendering section):

```vue src/components/ChatEntry.vue
<!-- Selection context menu -->
<SelectionMenu 
  :selectedText="selectedText"
  :position="selectionMenuPosition"
  :isVisible="showSelectionMenu"
  @copy="onSelectionCopy"
  @create-subtask="onSelectionCreateSubtask"
  @close="showSelectionMenu = false"
/>
```

And add this to the `data()` method in the `<script>` section:

```javascript src/components/ChatEntry.vue
data() {
  return {
    srcView: false,
    isRemove: false,
    improvementData: null,
    showDiff: false,
    showPRView: false,
    documentId: 'doc-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8),
    activeBranch: null,
    branchLoading: false,
    showSelectionMenu: false,
    selectionMenuPosition: { x: 0, y: 0 },
    selectedText: ''
  }
}
```

Add these methods to the `methods` section in ChatEntry.vue:

```javascript src/components/ChatEntry.vue
methods: {
  // ... existing methods ...

  onContentMouseUp() {
    const selection = window.getSelection()
    const selectedText = selection.toString().trim()

    if (selectedText.length > 0) {
      const range = selection.getRangeAt(0)
      const rect = range.getBoundingClientRect()

      this.selectedText = selectedText
      this.selectionMenuPosition = {
        x: rect.left + rect.width / 2 - 96,
        y: rect.bottom + 10
      }
      this.showSelectionMenu = true
    } else {
      this.showSelectionMenu = false
    }
  },

  onSelectionCopy(text) {
    this.copyTextToClipboard(text)
    this.$ui.showNotification('Copied to clipboard', 'success')
  },

  onSelectionCreateSubtask(text) {
    this.$emit('sub-task', {
      title: text.substring(0, 100),
      description: text,
      parentMessage: this.message
    })
  }
}
```

Add this to the template where the message content is displayed (in the contentArea div):

```vue src/components/ChatEntry.vue
<div 
  ref="contentArea"
  @copy.stop="onMessageCopy"
  @mouseup="onContentMouseUp"
  :class="[
    'max-w-full border-slate-300/20', 
    (isCollapsed === undefined ? displayMessage.hide : isCollapsed) 
      ? 'h-6 overflow-hidden' 
      : 'h-fit'
  ]"
>
```

## Summary of Changes

1. **Created SelectionMenu.vue** - A floating context menu component that appears near selected text
2. **Updated ChatEntry.vue** to:
   - Import the SelectionMenu component
   - Add state variables for tracking selection and menu visibility
   - Add `onContentMouseUp()` to detect text selection
   - Add `onSelectionCopy()` to copy selected text
   - Add `onSelectionCreateSubtask()` to emit sub-task event with selected text
   - Add `@mouseup` listener to the content area
   - Render the SelectionMenu component

The menu will automatically close when clicking outside or on the close button, and provides a clean DaisyUI-styled interface for user actions.

